  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  data:
    name: Stapes
    detail: 'The stapes (stirrup) is the smallest bone in the human body and the
      innermost ossicle of the middle ear.

      It connects the long process of
      the incus to the oval window of the inner ear, transmitting sound vibrations
      from the middle ear to the cochlea.'
